<p id="Sx1.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The author has no active funding.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="Sx1.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Conflicts of interests/Competing interests</h3>

<div id="Sx1.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Sx1.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The author has no relevant conflicting or competing interests.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Kernel-differentiation method</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We briefly go through the kernel-differentiation method, and explain its problem when applied to linear responses of high-dimensional systems with respect to diffusion coefficients.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1. </span>One-step results</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\gamma}_{0}\sim h^{\gamma}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\gamma}_{0}\sim h^{\gamma}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b^{\gamma}_{0}\sim k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b^{\gamma}_{0}\sim k</annotation></semantics></math>, the one-step dynamics is</p>
<table id="A1.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}x^{\gamma}_{1}=f^{\gamma}_{0}(x^{\gamma}_{0})+\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}(x^{\gamma}_{0})b_{0}.\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}x^{\gamma}_{1}=f^{\gamma}_{0}(x^{\gamma}_{0})+\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}(x^{\gamma}_{0})b_{0}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The most natural expression of <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h^{\gamma}_{1}(x_{1})=\int h^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})(\sigma^{\gamma}_{0})^{-M}(x_{0})k\left(\frac{x_{1}-f^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})}{\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})}\right)dx_{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h^{\gamma}_{1}(x_{1})=\int h^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})(\sigma^{\gamma}_{0})^{-M}(x_{0})k\left(\frac{x_{1}-f^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})}{\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})}\right)dx_{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Take derivative with respect to <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, then the probability kernel <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> will be differentiated, and we get the kernel-differentiation formula for one-step.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para"><span id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">[Kernel formula for one-step linear response]</p>
<table id="A1.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\log h^{\gamma}_{1}(x_{1})=\mathbb{E}\left[\delta\log h^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})-M\delta\log\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})-\frac{\nabla\log k(b_{0})}{\sigma_{0}(x_{0})}\left(\delta\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})b_{0}+\delta f^{\gamma}(x_{0})\right)\middle|x_{1}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\log h^{\gamma}_{1}(x_{1})=\mathbb{E}\left[\delta\log h^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})-M\delta\log\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})-\frac{\nabla\log k(b_{0})}{\sigma_{0}(x_{0})}\left(\delta\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})b_{0}+\delta f^{\gamma}(x_{0})\right)\middle|x_{1}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take derivative of <a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3.1. Divergence formula One-step system ‣ 3. Derivation of the divergence-kernel formula for linear responses ‣ Divergence-Kernel method for linear responses and diffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> with respect to <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\delta h^{\gamma}_{1}(x_{1})=\int\left(\frac{\delta h^{\gamma}_{0}}{h_{0}}(x_{0})-M\frac{\delta\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}}{\sigma_{0}}(x_{0})-\frac{\nabla k}{k}(b_{0})\left(\frac{\delta\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}}{\sigma_{0}}(x_{0})b_{0}+\frac{\delta f^{\gamma}_{0}}{\sigma_{0}}(x_{0})\right)\right)h_{0}(x_{0})\frac{k\left(b_{0}\right)}{\sigma^{M}(x_{0})}dx_{0},\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mi>M</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\delta h^{\gamma}_{1}(x_{1})=\int\left(\frac{\delta h^{\gamma}_{0}}{h_{0}}(x_{0})-M\frac{\delta\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}}{\sigma_{0}}(x_{0})-\frac{\nabla k}{k}(b_{0})\left(\frac{\delta\sigma^{\gamma}_{0}}{\sigma_{0}}(x_{0})b_{0}+\frac{\delta f^{\gamma}_{0}}{\sigma_{0}}(x_{0})\right)\right)h_{0}(x_{0})\frac{k\left(b_{0}\right)}{\sigma^{M}(x_{0})}dx_{0},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b_{0}=(x_{1}-f_{0}(x_{0}))/\sigma_{0}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>b</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b_{0}=(x_{1}-f_{0}(x_{0}))/\sigma_{0}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.
Divide both sides by <math id="A1.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{1}(x_{1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{1}(x_{1})</annotation></semantics></math> and apply the definition of the conditional expectation to prove the lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">The second term in <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1. One-step results ‣ Appendix A Kernel-differentiation method ‣ Divergence-Kernel method for linear responses and diffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> can be very large for high-dimensional noise since it involves <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>.
For now, we still use noise in all directions, so we try to avoid using the kernel formula for parameter derivative.
The kernel formula for the spatial derivative does not have terms involving <math id="A1.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">24</a>]</cite>, so we can still use that.
We will try to use low-dimensional noise in later papers, which will incur additional difficulties.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2. </span>Discrete-time many-steps </h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First by recursively apply <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1. One-step results ‣ Appendix A Kernel-differentiation method ‣ Divergence-Kernel method for linear responses and diffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, we can prove the following kernel-differentiation formula for linear response.
Here, if we set <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\sigma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\sigma=0</annotation></semantics></math>, this becomes the typical likelihood ratio formula.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para"><span id="A1.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A1.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">[N-step kernel-differentiation formula for linear responses]</p>
<table id="A1.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\log h^{\gamma}_{N}(x_{N})=\mathbb{E}\left[\delta\log h^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})-\sum_{n=0}^{N-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{n}(x_{n})}\left(M\delta\sigma^{\gamma}_{n}(x_{n})+\nabla\log k(b_{n})\left(\delta\sigma^{\gamma}_{n}(x_{n})b_{n}+\delta f^{\gamma}(x_{n})\right)\right)\middle|x_{N}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>N</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>b</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\log h^{\gamma}_{N}(x_{N})=\mathbb{E}\left[\delta\log h^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})-\sum_{n=0}^{N-1}\frac{1}{\sigma_{n}(x_{n})}\left(M\delta\sigma^{\gamma}_{n}(x_{n})+\nabla\log k(b_{n})\left(\delta\sigma^{\gamma}_{n}(x_{n})b_{n}+\delta f^{\gamma}(x_{n})\right)\right)\middle|x_{N}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3. </span>Formal continuous-time limit</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the continuous time limit, we first consider the time-discretized SDEs.
Note that if <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\sigma\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\sigma\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, then the two terms involve <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\sigma</annotation></semantics></math> in the kernel formula in <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1. One-step results ‣ Appendix A Kernel-differentiation method ‣ Divergence-Kernel method for linear responses and diffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> becomes <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> in each step, so the integration in time does not converge –
this is why likelihood ratio method always uses additive noise independent of the parameter <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the degenerate case where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\sigma\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\sigma\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>, <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2. Discrete-time many-steps ‣ Appendix A Kernel-differentiation method ‣ Divergence-Kernel method for linear responses and diffusion models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a> converges to the classical likelihood ratio method in continuous time.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para"><span id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">{lemma}</span>
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">[likelihood ratio formula for linear response of SDEs] 
If <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\sigma\equiv 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><mo>≡</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\sigma\equiv 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{split}\nabla\log h_{T}(x_{T})=\mathbb{E}\left[\delta\log h^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})+\int_{t=0}^{T}\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}(x_{t})}\delta F^{\gamma}(x_{n})\cdot dB\middle|x_{N}\right].\end{split}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable displaystyle="true"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mi>T</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>F</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>⋅</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{split}\nabla\log h_{T}(x_{T})=\mathbb{E}\left[\delta\log h^{\gamma}_{0}(x_{0})+\int_{t=0}^{T}\frac{1}{\sigma_{t}(x_{t})}\delta F^{\gamma}(x_{n})\cdot dB\middle|x_{N}\right].\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
